## Queue
{% if queue == 'sync' %}

Queued jobs are **not** processed in the background: `QUEUE_CONNECTION=sync` runs each job inline, during the web request that dispatched it. There is no `worker` service in any stack. To get background processing, regenerate the project with `queue=database` or `queue=redis`.
{%- else %}

Queued jobs (`QUEUE_CONNECTION={{ queue }}`) are processed by the `worker` service in every stack, which reuses the app image. The dev stack uses a real queue too (not `sync`), so jobs behave locally as they do once deployed.

| Stack | Worker command | Notes |
|---|---|---|
{% if horizon -%}
| Dev | `php artisan horizon` | Does not reload your code between jobs: run `php artisan horizon:terminate` after editing job code |
| Staging | `php artisan horizon --environment=production` | Runs as `www-data`; starts once `app` is healthy, i.e. migrations have run. `--environment=production` because `config/horizon.php` only defines the `production` and `local` supervisors, and staging runs with `APP_ENV=staging` |
| Production | `php artisan horizon` | Runs as `www-data`; starts once `app` is healthy, i.e. migrations have run |
{%- else -%}
| Dev | `php artisan queue:listen --tries=1 --timeout=0` | Reloads your code on every job |
| Staging / production | `php artisan queue:work --sleep=3 --tries=3 --max-time=3600` | Runs as `www-data`; starts once `app` is healthy, i.e. migrations have run |
{%- endif %}

Staging/production worker settings (shell-exported env vars, like the other secrets):

| Variable | Default | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| `WORKER_STOP_GRACE_PERIOD` | `90s` | How long `docker compose stop worker` (and a deploy) waits for the running job to finish. Must exceed the longest job timeout{% if horizon %} (the supervisors' `timeout` in `config/horizon.php` is 60 s by default){% else %} (`queue:work` defaults to 60 s){% endif %}, or the job is killed mid-run |
{% if queue == 'redis' -%}
| `REDIS_PASSWORD` | _(required)_ | Password of the staging/production Redis; `docker compose` refuses to start without it |

Redis is reached through the pure-PHP `predis/predis` client (installed for you, so the image needs no `phpredis` extension). In staging/production it is password-protected and persists its data in the `redis_data_*` volume; the dev Redis has no password.
{%- else %}
Jobs are stored in the `jobs` table, created by the starter kit's migration. To use Redis instead, regenerate the project with `queue=redis`.
{%- endif %}
{%- endif %}
{% if horizon %}

## Horizon

The `worker` service runs [Laravel Horizon](https://laravel.com/docs/horizon), which supervises the Redis queue workers; its settings (supervisors, processes, timeouts, retries) live in `config/horizon.php`.

Dashboard: [`http://localhost:{{ app_port }}/horizon`](http://localhost:{{ app_port }}/horizon)

Outside the `local` environment (staging, production) the dashboard is only reachable by users allowed by the `viewHorizon` gate in `app/Providers/HorizonServiceProvider.php`. It ships with an empty list of allowed emails, so add yours there before deploying.

If a job can run longer than 60 s, raise `timeout` for its supervisor in `config/horizon.php` (keeping `retry_after` in `config/queue.php` above it) **and** raise `WORKER_STOP_GRACE_PERIOD` above it: otherwise `docker compose stop worker` kills the job once the grace period runs out.
{% endif %}

